    {
      "blockId": "tour:itinerary_text:b9ad3e14216c2f08",
      "field": "itinerary.text",
      "sourceTextSha256": "bd7af463c26641766df051577928b0d29ec2d3db23626a283ec0a2b6d7353209",
      "text": "After breakfast, you will visit Rábida, known as the Red Island. The colour of its shore comes from the oxidation of old, porous lava.\n\nYou can choose to walk around the island, take one of the 8 two-person kayaks or a stand-up paddleboard, go snorkelling, or watch hundreds of sea lions on the beach.\n\nAfter lunch, a talk on the evolution of Darwin's finches will take place in the panoramic lounge. The yacht will then head to the northern coast of Santa Cruz, to Caleta Tortuga Negra. This mangrove estuary is home to sea turtles. You will explore by boat without landing. From the boat, you may see green sea turtles and 3 shark species: black, Galapagos and blue sharks.\n\nIn the evening, you will continue exploring Ecuadorian cuisine with Andean touches in Pedro Miguel Schiaffino's interpretation. Dishes include Galapagueña lobster rolls wrapped in lettuce leaves with acevichado sauce.",
      "provenance": {
        "kind": "ai_translation",
        "runId": "ada-en-704e3e13-mw25t7t2",
        "model": "GPT-6",
        "wordAbsenceReason": "The verified Word has only a day 6 route image naming Rabida and Caleta Tortuga Negra; it contains no detailed day 6 programme, kayaks, finch lecture, turtle/shark passage or lobster-roll dinner. Translate this assigned day narrative from RU."
      }
